## 9. Letter Shift Coding

The simplest coding method is shifting letters.

Example:

```text
CAT → DBU
```

Convert:

```text
C → D = +1
A → B = +1
T → U = +1
```

Therefore the rule is:

```text
Every letter +1
```

Apply to:

```text
DOG
```

```text
D → E
O → P
G → H
```

Answer:

```text
EPH
```

---

## 10. +2 Coding

Example:

```text
CAT → ECV
```

Because:

```text
C + 2 = E
A + 2 = C
T + 2 = V
```

Therefore:

```text
DOG → FQI
```

---

## 11. -1 Coding

Example:

```text
DOG → CNF
```

because:

```text
D → C
O → N
G → F
```

Rule:

```text
Each letter -1
```

---

## 12. Different Shifts

Sometimes every position has a different shift.

Example:

```text
CAT → DBW
```

Compare:

```text
C → D = +1
A → B = +1
T → W = +3
```

The rule may depend on:

- position
- letter
- vowel/consonant
- alphabet position
- alternating pattern

Never assume all letters use the same shift.

---

## 13. Alternating Shift Coding

Example:

```text
ABCDE → BZDCF
```

Maybe:

```text
Position 1: +1
Position 2: -1
Position 3: +1
Position 4: -1
Position 5: +1
```

Test:

```text
A → B
B → A
C → D
D → C
E → F
```

So:

```text
BADCF
```

The exact example must always be checked against the supplied pattern.

---

## 14. Position-Based Shift

A common advanced pattern:

```text
1st letter +1
2nd letter +2
3rd letter +3
4th letter +4
...
```

Example:

```text
ABCD
```

Apply:

```text
A + 1 = B
B + 2 = D
C + 3 = F
D + 4 = H
```

Therefore:

```text
ABCD → BDFH
```

---

## 15. Reverse Position Shift

Another pattern:

```text
1st letter +4
2nd letter +3
3rd letter +2
4th letter +1
```

Example:

```text
ABCD
```

gives:

```text
A → E
B → E
C → E
D → E
```

Result:

```text
EEEE
```

This illustrates why the position of a letter may matter more than its identity.

---

## 16. Wrap-Around Rule

Alphabet shifts do not stop at Z.

They usually wrap around.

Example:

```text
Z + 1 = A
```

Likewise:

```text
Y + 3 = B
```

because:

```text
Y → Z → A → B
```

---

## 17. Circular Alphabet Diagram

```text
             A
        Z           B
      Y               C
     X                 D
    W                   E
    V                   F
    U                   G
     T                 H
      S               I
        R           J
             ...
```

Think of the alphabet as a circle.

Mathematically:

```text
new_position = ((old_position - 1 + shift) mod 26) + 1
```

---
